Arrange rooms automatically using furniture you own. Choose any combination of Comfort, Stimulation, Health, Mutation and Appeal, with optional Min and Max values.

In furniture-placement mode, click a room's wand. Choose your stats, click Calculate, compare the results, then Apply.

The interface follows your game language: English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, Korean, Japanese or Simplified Chinese.

[list]
[*]Pin pieces you want to keep in place, and optionally include utility furniture such as food storage boxes.
[*]Return furniture from one room or the whole house with one click.
[*]Undo the last mod action before manually moving furniture or leaving the scene.
[/list]
Only the selected room and loose inventory are used. Nothing is taken from other rooms. Min targets are best-effort; Max values are limits. The search reports its best found layout, not a guaranteed optimum. Mouse and keyboard required.

[b]Installation[/b]
Requires Windows, Mewgenics 1.1.21239 (Steam build 25143593) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mewgenics/mods/218]Mewjector[/url] API 3 or newer. Close the game and back up your saves first.

[b]Vortex:[/b] Install, enable and deploy the ZIP. Enable Auto Furniture in Load Order, then launch through Vortex.
[b]Mewtator:[/b] Import the ZIP, enable Auto Furniture and DLL Mod Support, then launch through Mewtator.

The [url=https://github.com/anitosq/mewgenics-mods/tree/main/mods/auto-furniture]guide[/url] covers manual installation, controls and removal. Removing the mod leaves your furniture in place.

